From 158d13bcd22dac3797dadee45b1d8f983277a675 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 10:53:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2289/2312] media: verisilicon: add AVS1 and AVS+ decoding on
 the RK3588 AVS+ decoder

The RK3588 has an AVS+ decoder at 0xfdb51000, next to the VPU121: a
Hantro G1 style decoder in AVS mode (11), with the AVS+ (GY/T 257.1,
profile 0x48) extensions: AEC entropy coding, weighting quantisation,
enhanced field B pictures and no forward reference P pictures. It also
decodes JiZhun (GB/T 20090.2, profile 0x20) streams. It shares the
interrupt line, clocks, power domain and IOMMU with the VDPU2 decoder of
the VPU121.

Drive it as one more decoder of the VPU121 device, when the device tree
describes its "avsd" register range, with the stateless AVS uAPI
(V4L2_PIX_FMT_AVS_FRAME):

- the AVS formats and controls are exposed by a variant of the VPU121
  that is selected at probe time, so older device trees are unaffected;
- the interrupt handler of the shared line checks the AVS+ decoder
  status first and leaves the interrupts it didn't raise to the VDPU2
  handler;
- jobs run in the same queue as the VDPU2 decoder and the VEPU2
  encoder, so the blocks never run at the same time;
- a field coded picture takes two hardware runs in one job: the second
  field is started from the interrupt of the first, at the first slice
  start code after the point where the hardware stopped. The bitstream is
  therefore mapped in the kernel for this variant;
- the motion vectors of I and P pictures, used by the direct mode of the
  following B pictures, are stored after the picture in its buffer;
- the reference distances and their inverses, the field offsets and the
  weighting quantisation parameters are derived from the picture control.

The identification register is read and logged before the first AVS
decode, and decoding is refused when it reads 0 or all ones.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
